# SHAKE -- family: OPPOSITES.
# Idea: the bright, noisy small percussion the slot lacked, on the voice's
# shaker model (band-passed, optionally sparse noise; no pitch). The middle
# of every macro is that model at its default values, the shaker of the
# CLASSIC BASSHAUS demo; each macro runs it a long way both ways:
#   TONE    dark: the band at 2.5 kHz, more resonant, no dry hiss .. bright:
#           the band at 11 kHz, open, with air on top
#   LENGTH  tight: an 8 ms tick .. long: a 250 ms wash (the tight end is
#           lifted, the long end held down)
#   GRAIN   sand: dense white grains, a wide band, a little dry hiss ..
#           beads: sparse grains through a narrow, ringing band, a little
#           longer (a rattle, the nearest this voice gets to jingles)
#   STROKE  soft: a slow swell into the hit, darker, a little longer, clean
#           .. hard: an instant attack, brighter, driven, dry noise on top
#           (the drive's loudness is trimmed back)
# Corners to try: TIGHT + HARD + BRIGHT is a closed-hat tick; LONG + SAND +
# SOFT a cabasa push; BEADS + LONG + BRIGHT a tambourine-ish rattle (no
# metal: the shaker model has no partials to ring).
# Every parameter is latched at the next hit on this voice, so a sweep is
# heard hit by hit (fine on a 16th line).
# Try: TONE on X, GRAIN on Y on 16ths with ghost notes; then STROKE on the
# accents.
voice perc
name SHAKE
about "A shaker on the SHKR model."
tilt x TONE                   # tilt: brighter / darker
tilt y GRAIN                  # tilt: sand / beads
base modl=shkr tune=64 decay=64 tone=64 bend=64 harm=64 noise=64 drive=32 lvl=108

macro TONE 0.5 "DARK" "BRIGHT"
  tune     0:0 0.5:64 1:127
  tone     add 0:24 0.5:0 1:-12
  noise    add 0:-30 0.5:0 1:24
  trim     0:-0.5 0.5:0 0.75:1 1:2.5

macro LENGTH 0.5 "TIGHT" "LONG"
  decay    0:0 0.5:64 1:124
  trim     0:4.5 0.25:2 0.5:0 0.75:-2.5 1:-3.5

macro GRAIN 0.5 "SAND" "BEADS"
  harm     0:0 0.5:64 1:110
  tone     add 0:-34 0.5:0 1:60
  noise    add 0:20 0.5:0 1:-40
  decay    add 0:0 0.5:0 1:16

macro STROKE 0.5 "SOFT" "HARD"
  bend     0:110 0.5:64 1:0
  decay    add 0:12 0.5:0 1:-8
  drive    0:10 0.5:32 1:90
  noise    add 0:-30 0.5:0 1:40
  tune     add 0:-14 0.5:0 1:14
  trim     0:0.5 0.5:0 0.75:-4 1:-7.5
